{"repositoryId":994489055,"availability":"available","full":"InternRobotics/AnySplat","name":"AnySplat","description":"[SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 (ACM TOG)] AnySplat: Feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting from Unconstrained Views","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":955,"forks":58,"created":"2025-06-02T02:39:22Z","updated":"2025-12-22T06:12:51Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/alexnasa/AnySplat","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.025Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.025Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.025Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.025Z","stars":955,"forks":58}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lihan Jiang, Yucheng Mao, Linning Xu, Tao Lu, Kerui Ren, Yichen Jin, Xudong Xu, Mulin Yu, Jiangmiao Pang, Feng Zhao, Dahua Lin, Bo Dai†","Starting from a set of uncalibrated images, a transformer-based geometry encoder is followed by three decoder heads: FG, FD, and FC, which respectively predict the Gaussian parameters (μ, σ, r, s, c), the depth map D, and the camera poses p. These outputs are used to construct a set of pixel-wise 3D Gaussians, which is then voxelized into pre-voxel 3D Gaussians with the proposed Differentiable Voxelization module. From the voxelized 3D Gaussians, multi-view images and depth maps are subsequently rendered. The rendered images are supervised using an RGB loss against the ground truth image,…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/InternRobotics/AnySplat/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f28f8d21bd3d932e1603a394c65a5f7a7cf7056ba905a6b7224f70d73183b119","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.089Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T12:31:37.089Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Lihan Jiang, Yucheng Mao, Linning Xu, Tao Lu, Kerui Ren, Yichen Jin, Xudong Xu, Mulin Yu, Jiangmiao Pang, Feng Zhao, Dahua Lin, Bo Dai†","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/I